\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\cf1\ul\b\fs40 Nginx\par
\cf5\ulnone\b0\fs28 Nginx Load Balancer: Distributes traffic across the three Apache servers.\par
\cf1\ul\b\fs40\par
\cf0\ulnone\b0\fs22\par
Create another VM for the Nginx load balancer.\par
security group----add rule----80\par
Install Nginx:\par
\cf3\fs24 sudo apt update\par
sudo apt install nginx\par
\cf0\fs22 Configure Nginx to balance traffic across the three Apache servers:\par
Edit the Nginx configuration file \par
Go to \cf3\fs28 /etc/nginx/sites-available/default\cf0\fs22\par
Replace with the actual IP addresses of your Apache servers.\par
\par
\cf1\fs28 upstream backend \{\par
    server 44.202.113.38;\par
    server 54.173.204.163;\par
    server 44.202.2.213;\par
\}\par
server \{\par
    listen 80;\par
    location / \{\par
        proxy_pass {\cf0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK http://backend }}{\fldrslt{http://backend\ul0\cf0}}}}\f0\fs28 ;\par
        proxy_set_header Host $host;\par
        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;\par
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;\par
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;\par
    \}\par
\}\par
\cf0\fs22 Test the Setup:\par
\cf3\fs28 sudo nginx -t\par
\cf0\fs22 Restart Nginx:\par
Apply the changes by restarting Nginx:\par
\cf3\fs24 sudo systemctl restart nginx\par
\cf0\fs22 Access the load balancer\rquote s IP address in a web browser.while refreshing.....\par
